   "html": "<h2>14.1 Assessment Format</h2>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\"><table>\n<colgroup>\n<col />\n<col />\n<col />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Part</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Format</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Weightage</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Part A: Knowledge Quiz</strong></td>\n<td>20 multiple-choice questions</td>\n<td>60%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Part B: Phishing-Spotting Practical</strong></td>\n<td>5 real-world style messages: classify and justify</td>\n<td>40%</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<p><strong>Passing score:</strong> 50% overall. Candidates who pass receive the <strong>Certified Phishing Prevention Specialist (CPPS)</strong> certificate. Suggested validity: 2 years, since phishing techniques evolve quickly.</p>\n<h2>Certificate Criteria</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><p>Completion of all modules (0 to 13).</p></li>\n<li><p>Score of 50% or above in the combined assessment.</p></li>\n<li><p>Certificate issued in the name of the candidate with a unique certificate ID and issue date.</p></li>\n</ul>\n",
